From fde1f2def78d0fdd06c7a87e181e804c44267c42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 07:53:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] qwen4exp/ggml: fused INDEXER_POOL op (pool+norm) for the
 sparse-decode path

New GGML_OP_INDEXER_POOL replaces the per-op get_rows + r-slice cont/add loop +
scale(1/r) + rms_norm chain (~10 kernels/layer) with ONE kernel, env-gated on
for single-token decode via GGML_CUDA_QSA_INDEXER_POOL=1 (default OFF until the
remaining score-side fusion lands).  The kernel replicates the per-op F32
arithmetic byte-identically: bf16->f32 cache gather (ggml bits<<16), sequential
member adds, scalar 1/r scale, and the 256/1024-thread rms_norm reduction order
from norm.cu - same-seed decode text is byte-identical ON vs OFF.

gfx1201 (3x R9700, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ4_XS, tensor bf16, interleaved):
decode @d32768 39.7 -> 42.1 (+6.0%); @d65536 35.5 -> 38.9 (+9.6%).
Plumbing: enum/name/symbol/builders, backend-choice skip, meta-backend mirrored
split, CUDA dispatch + supported, RPC proto bump.  CPU fallback deferred (op is
decode-gated GPU-only until adopted).
